            "end": 392,
            "source_id": "Schr\u00f6der\u2013Bernstein theorem",
            "start": 0,
            "text": "In set theory, the Schr\u00f6der\u2013Bernstein theorem (named after Felix Bernstein and Ernst Schr\u00f6der, also known as Cantor\u2013Bernstein theorem, or Cantor\u2013Schr\u00f6der\u2013Bernstein after Georg Cantor who first published it without proof) states that, if there exist injective functions \"f\" : \"A\" \u2192 \"B\" and \"g\" : \"B\" \u2192 \"A\" between the sets \"A\" and \"B\" , then there exists a bijective function \"h\" : \"A\" \u2192 \"B\" ."
          }
